# SRG-APP-000179-WSR-000111  -  CAT II
# The web server must use cryptographic modules that meet the requirements
# of applicable federal laws, Executive Orders, directives, policies,
# regulations, standards, and guidance for such authentication.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000179-WSR-000111
group:           V-206391
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-000803
control_rev5:    IA-7

contribution:    For authentication, Splunk can run in FIPS mode so that every
                 cryptographic operation uses the validated module, store passwords under a
                 SHA-based hash, and serve the logon only over TLS 1.2.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.
governs:         splunk-launch.conf - Environment settings read before Splunk starts, including whether it
                 starts in FIPS mode.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
check:           authentication.conf [authentication] passwordHashAlgorithm matches ^SHA(256|512)-crypt(-[0-9]{4,})?$
check:           web.conf [settings] enableSplunkWebSSL equals true
check:           web.conf [settings] sslVersions matches (^|,)\s*tls1\.2\s*(,|$)
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS equals 1 -> splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
vendor:          authentication.conf [authentication] passwordHashAlgorithm https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
vendor:          splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/splunk-launch.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] enableSplunkWebSSL https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] sslVersions https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/secure-splunk-platform-communications-with-transport-layer-security-certificates/configure-tls-protocol-version-support-for-secure-connections-between-splunk-platform-instances
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The FIPS 140-2 validated cryptographic module shipped with the platform
                 and the host kernel FIPS state
external:        Cryptographic modules used by an LDAP or SAML identity provider when it
                 performs the authentication, including the OpenLDAP client configuration
                 named in SPLK-CL-000320
external:        FIPS mode must be set before first start
                 (splunk-launch.conf.spec:110-130), so enabling it later is a reinstall or
                 upgrade

citation:        SPLK-CL-000390 check and fix text (FIPS mode) and SPLK-CL-000430 fix text
                 (tls1.2 pin, with the note that the instance must operate in FIPS mode to
                 limit the algorithms allowed); splunk-launch.conf.spec:110-130;
                 authentication.conf.spec:58-80; web.conf.spec:70-73 (enableSplunkWebSSL,
                 default false), web.conf.spec:239-250 (sslVersions vocabulary; ssl3 always
                 disabled in FIPS mode)
finding:         splunk-launch.conf does not set SPLUNK_FIPS = 1, passwordHashAlgorithm is
                 outside the SHA families, or Splunk Web is not serving over TLS 1.2, so
                 authentication is not performed with validated cryptographic modules to
                 the extent the product allows.
